# Backend (module root)
shed-server
*.exe

# Frontend
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.env*.local

# `frontend/package-lock.json` was listed here and is tracked anyway — an
# ignore rule does not apply to a file already in the index, so it stayed
# committed and nobody noticed the contradiction. CI resolves it: `npm ci`
# needs the lockfile, and a run that silently resolved a different dependency
# tree than the one tested here would be worth nothing. It is checked in on
# purpose.

# Playwright. The frozen reference renders are generated on the machine that
# checks them and are deliberately not committed, so a clone's first `npm run
# test:e2e` writes its own baselines and fails; the second run is the one that
# means something. `test-results/` is where a failure leaves the actual, the
# expected and the diff to look at.
frontend/e2e/__screenshots__/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

